      \field{abstract}{We study the {N}ash Social Welfare problem: Given n agents with valuation functions vi : 2[m] → R+, partition [m] into S1, …, Sn so as to maximize [EQUATION]. The problem has been shown to admit a constant-factor approximation for additive, budget-additive, and piecewise linear concave separable valuations; the case of submodular valuations is open.We provide a [EQUATION]-approximation of the optimal value for several classes of submodular valuations: coverage, sums of matroid rank functions, and certain matching-based valuations.}
